<title>USA: Net Lease Management says buys K Mart centers.</title>
<headline>Net Lease Management says buys K Mart centers.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net Lease Management Partners LLC said it has purchased from K Mart Corp two large distribution centers for a total of $74.3 million.</p>
<p>Net Lease Management said it completed the purchase March 25 and leased the centers back to K Mart.  The centers, in Greensboro, N.C. and Brighton, Colo., total approximately 2,800,000 square feet, the company said.</p>
<p>Net Lease Management is a newly formed entity whose largest shareholder is United Capital Corp. Other members include Brentwood Capital LLC, Koffman Group and the Holtzman Family Partnership.</p>
</text>
